=== PARITY (web source reproduced end-to-end) ===
  - Data sources (web useTranslation + useUnits): bound through the P1/S8 seam
    BatteryRangeChartsSource→Model. The web component takes `state: VehicleState` +
    `drives: Drive[]?` props and reads `useUnits().unitPrefs.distance`; the native
    source composes vehicle state + recent drives + the distance unit into one
    coalesced update. No HTTP in the view.
  - Composition (web two `GlassPanel` panels, grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2):
      • Battery Overview -> glass panel w/ Battery icon + title; RadialGauge
        (web RadialGauge value=battery_level color=batteryColor) -> BatteryRangeGauge
        tinted by the battery-health tone (status success/warning/danger tokens =
        canonical equivalents of #10b981/#f59e0b/#ef4444); two tiles (web inner
        GlassPanel + AnimatedNumber) Battery "%" + Range "<n> <unit>" (0 dp);
        Current/Remaining BarMark on a fixed 0…100 scale (web Bar, CHART_COLORS[0]).
      • Drive Distance Trend -> glass panel w/ route icon + title; two overlapping
        gradient AreaMarks (distance CHART_COLORS[0], duration CHART_COLORS[1]) +
        stroke lines + legend, OR the empty row (web EmptyState
        `vehicles.detail.noDriveData`) when there are no drives — mirroring the web
        `driveChartData.length > 0 ? <AreaChart/> : <EmptyState/>`.
  - SI → display: BatteryRangeChartsMath.distanceFromSI reproduces the web
    `lib/unitConversion.ts` meter constants (mi=1609.344, km=1000, ft=0.3048);
    fmtNumber reproduces `lib/numberFormat.ts` (grouped, half-up, 0 dp); formatDate
    reproduces `lib/dateFormat.ts` short date ("Apr 4, 2025"). The drive memo
    rounds distance/duration and reverses to chronological order (web `.reverse()`).
  - States (ALL rendered, each with a #if DEBUG preview + a model/projection unit
    test): loading (skeleton) · content (battery panel + trend) · content-no-drives
    (trend empty row) · empty (resolved no state) · error (retry) · stale (chip +
    auto-refresh + banner) · offline (chip + banner, cached battery/trend kept).
  - i18n (P1/S10): web keys preserved verbatim — common.current/remaining/battery/
    range/distance/duration + vehicles.detail.batteryOverview/driveTrend/noDriveData;
    native chrome namespaced batteryRange.* (live/stale/offline/banners/loading/empty/
    error/retry/axis titles/a11y nouns). Every code-referenced key is declared in
